# Why this empty directory must exist in the repo
#
# `docker-compose.yml` bind-mounts the host directory
# `./docker/postgres/data` into the postgres container at
# `/var/lib/postgresql/data`. Docker auto-creates missing bind-mount
# source directories on Linux, but only on some Docker engine versions
# and only when the parent path is writable. On a fresh GitHub-hosted
# runner (ubuntu-latest) the first `docker compose up postgres` will:
#
#   1. Try to bind `./docker/postgres/data` from the workspace root.
#   2. If the dir is missing AND the engine refuses auto-create,
#      fail with: `error while mounting volume ... source directory
#      does not exist`.
#
# To make smoke runs reproducible the smoke workflow explicitly does
# `mkdir -p docker/postgres/data` BEFORE `docker compose up` (see
# `.github/workflows/smoke.yml`). This .gitkeep is the canonical proof
# in-repo that the path is expected to exist; it is intentionally the
# only file inside the directory because postgres manages the rest of
# the contents itself at runtime.
#
# This directory IS listed in `.gitignore` because we do NOT want to
# commit database data. The `.gitkeep` file is force-added by the
# smoke workflow's first commit and is otherwise harmless.
